<Base title="Terms of use | Chandragiri guide" description="Scope of an independent guide: sources, operation, tickets, map and weather limitations." noindex lang="en">
  <section class="section"><div class="shell prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p>This is an independent, unofficial, non-profit travel and educational guide. We do not operate the cable car, temple or resort, and we do not sell or reserve tickets.</p>

    <h2>Acceptance of terms</h2>
    <p>By accessing or using this site you agree to be bound by these terms. If you disagree with any part, please do not use the site.</p>

    <h2>Use of service</h2>
    <p>Ticket rates, currency, eligibility and operating times shown in sources are as of the review date, not a guarantee of the latest booking or current service. Operator schedule differences are separated on the page; confirm the final ticket, upward and downward service directly with the operator.</p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>The text, logo and design of this site (unless stated otherwise) are the property of the site operator and may not be used, copied or distributed without permission. The illustrative image is not a real station photo, building design or exact map and is from a CC0 source. Names/marks of Chandragiri Hills, the cable car operator, the temple or the resort belong to their respective owners.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>We are not liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or consequential damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, this site or its information. Map location references are not a surveyed entrance, boarding point or barrier-free route. Weather is a regional model and does not confirm wind, visibility, maintenance or safe operation of the whole line.</p>

    <p class="small">Reviewed: 2026-11-09.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
